# Shipped workflows. A home changes or adds any of them in config/workflows (same lines); a name there wins.
# <name>: <spec>     a spec is stages split by ">", steps that run at once split by "+", a count as "*N".
# <name>: off        removes a shipped name in this home.
# A step is a kind (worker, recon(quick|standard|deep), critic, owner(plan-approval), fanout, war-room(fast|full), muster(survey|light|full|complete))
# or any name in these files. A kind is also a one-step workflow of the same name.
scout: recon(quick)
deep: recon(deep) > critic
blitz: owner(plan-approval) > fanout
scout-worker: scout > owner > worker
deep-slices: deep > blitz
war-room-blitz: war-room(fast) > blitz
war-room-full-blitz: war-room(full) > blitz
war-room-lite-blitz: deep > blitz
discovery-first: war-room(fast) > muster(full) > war-room(full) > blitz
muster-first: muster(full) > war-room(full) > blitz
muster-only: muster(light) > blitz
# pick <test> <value>: <name>, first match wins; a home file with any pick line replaces all of these
pick title-tag [discovery-first]: discovery-first
pick title-tag [muster-first]: muster-first
pick title-tag [muster-only]: muster-only
pick title-tag [design-ux]: scout-worker
pick title-has war room: war-room-blitz
pick kind recon: deep-slices
pick label plan: deep-slices
pick any: worker
limit count: 30
limit steps: 64
angles: smallest change | strongest guarantees | outside prior art first
